target/

# Cargo.lock IS committed: this is a proof of concept pinned to a binius64 git
# revision, and its published benchmarks are only reproducible if the whole
# dependency graph is pinned too, not just the direct dependency.
spikes/*/web/*.wasm
spikes/*/web/*.js

# wasm-bindgen output for the browser demo. Generated by web/build.sh, 3.4 MB, and
# would go stale against the source without anyone noticing. A committed binary nobody
# can tie to the source is also the wrong thing to ask people to trust on a page whose
# whole claim is that their seed stays local.
web/pkg/
